# Local secrets, wherever they end up.
#
# Path-anchored rules are not enough on their own: these lived under functions/
# before the backend moved to worker/, and a directory-scoped ignore stops
# applying the moment the directory it names is deleted — which is exactly when
# `git add -A` would sweep the key in. Matching by filename anywhere means a
# future move cannot un-ignore a credential.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
**/.env.local
**/.env.*.local
**/.dev.vars
**/.dev.vars.*
!**/.dev.vars.example
